              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn app/db.py, update set_receipt_template at line 71 to reject Jinja control delimiters before persisting the template string.\n\n### Suggested fix\n    return row[\"receipt_template\"] if row else None\r\n\r\n\r\ndef set_receipt_template(restaurant_id, template):\r\n    if any(token in template for token in (\"{{\", \"{%\", \"{#\")):\r\n        raise ValueError(\"receipt template must be inert text\")\r\n\r\n    db = get_db()\r\n    db.execute(\r\n        \"UPDATE restaurants SET receipt_template = ? WHERE id = ?\",\r\n        (template, restaurant_id),\r\n    )\r\n    db.commit()\r\n\r\n\r\n# --- Menu ----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\n### Rationale\nBlocking Jinja expression, statement, and comment delimiters prevents attacker-supplied input from being stored as executable template syntax, so later render_template_string calls receive inert text instead of template code.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, submit a template such as {{ 7*7 }} through the receipts editor and observe that the value is stored and later evaluated during receipt rendering. After the change, the same input should be rejected with a validation error, while plain receipt text without Jinja delimiters should still be stored and rendered as literal text.",
