            "summary": "`set_receipt_template()` stores the caller-provided `template` string into `restaurants.receipt_template` at `app/db.py:74-75`. The scanner flagged this because the stored value is described elsewhere in the project metadata as later being passed to Flask/Jinja `render_template_string`, which would treat the stored text as executable template syntax rather than inert content. This becomes a security issue if an authenticated merchant can submit arbitrary template text through the receipts editor and the application later renders that stored value in a normal Jinja context.",
