            "annotatedSource": "28: def detail(order_id):\n# [FLOW] The handler derives the current merchant identity used to scope the template lookup to one restaurant.\n29:     user = current_user()\n30:     order = db.get_order(order_id)\n31:     if order is None or order[\"restaurant_id\"] != user[\"restaurant_id\"]:\n32:         flash(\"Order not found.\")\n33:         return redirect(url_for(\"orders.board\"))\n34: \n35:     restaurant = db.get_restaurant(user[\"restaurant_id\"])\n# [ENTRY] A receipt template string previously stored for the merchant's restaurant is loaded from the database without restriction on Jinja syntax.\n36:     template = db.get_receipt_template(user[\"restaurant_id\"]) or (\n37:         \"{{ restaurant.name }}\\n\"\n38:         \"Order #{{ order.id }}\\n\"\n39:         \"Total: {{ total }}\\n\"\n40:         \"Thanks for ordering with Caldova!\"\n41:     )\n42:     total = format_price(order[\"total_cents\"])\n# [FLAG] The scanner flagged the call that renders the database-backed template text as a Jinja template on the server.\n# [SINK] render_template_string evaluates the loaded template with order, restaurant, and total in scope.\n>>>43:     rendered_receipt = render_template_string(\n44:         template, order=order, restaurant=restaurant, total=total\n45:     )\n46: \n47:     return render_template(\n48:         \"order_detail.html\",\n49:         order=order,\n50:         restaurant=restaurant,\n51:         format_price=format_price,\n52:         receipt=rendered_receipt,\n53:         template=template,\n54:     )",
