                "verification": "Before the change, store a receipt template such as '{{ 7*7 }}' or a Jinja object-traversal payload for a restaurant and open /orders/<order_id>; the expression is evaluated by Jinja in the receipt output. After the change, unsupported Jinja expressions should remain inert text while the supported placeholders '{{ restaurant.name }}', '{{ order.id }}', and '{{ total }}' still render to the restaurant name, order id, and formatted total."
