                "text": "### Description\nIn app/routes/orders.py, replace the dynamic Jinja evaluation in detail() at lines 42-45 with literal substitution for the supported receipt placeholders instead of calling render_template_string on merchant-stored text.\n\n### Suggested fix\n        \"Total: {{ total }}\\n\"\r\n        \"Thanks for ordering with Caldova!\"\r\n    )\r\n    total = format_price(order[\"total_cents\"])\r\n    rendered_receipt = (\r\n        template.replace(\"{{ restaurant.name }}\", str(restaurant[\"name\"]))\r\n        .replace(\"{{ order.id }}\", str(order[\"id\"]))\r\n        .replace(\"{{ total }}\", total)\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    return render_template(\r\n        \"order_detail.html\",\r\n\n### Rationale\nLiteral replacement expands only the explicitly allowed tokens and never parses the merchant-supplied template as executable Jinja, so template expressions are treated as data rather than code.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, store a receipt template such as '{{ 7*7 }}' or a Jinja object-traversal payload for a restaurant and open /orders/<order_id>; the expression is evaluated by Jinja in the receipt output. After the change, unsupported Jinja expressions should remain inert text while the supported placeholders '{{ restaurant.name }}', '{{ order.id }}', and '{{ total }}' still render to the restaurant name, order id, and formatted total."
