            "dataFlowTrace": "`session.get(\"user_id\")` -> `db.get_user` -> `current_user`\n\n- **[ENTRY]** `session.get(\"user_id\")`  `app/auth.py:32`\n  current_user pulls user_id from the Flask session, which is attacker-controlled if the deployment keeps the documented default signing secret.\n- **[FLOW]** `db.get_user`  `app/auth.py:33`\n  The session-derived user_id is passed to the database lookup, and any matching row becomes g.user without additional authentication checks here.\n- **[FLAG]** `current_user`  `app/auth.py:40`\n  login_required uses the resolved g.user value as the route-level authentication decision.",
            "dataFlowValidation": "strict",
