            "prerequisites": "- **Deployment conditions:** The issue depends on the admin route being exposed in the running application without an authentication or role check.\n- **Default vs optional code:** The trust-boundary context describes the admin blueprint as part of the public HTTP surface, not an optional extension.\n- **Trust boundary crossed:** The reported boundary is from an **unauthenticated remote web client** to an administrative state-changing operation.\n- **Attacker access assumed:** A remote caller able to send HTTP requests to `/admin/restaurants/<restaurant_id>/toggle`.\n- **Code behavior:** The helper itself is by design a database primitive that performs an `UPDATE`; the access-control question is whether callers are restricted before reaching it.\n- **Project context:** The supplied security concerns explicitly describe the admin restaurant listing and toggle routes as exposed without authentication or role checks.\n- **Related CVEs:** The listed CVE (`CVE-2016-10745`) concerns Jinja2 sandbox escape and is not similar to this missing-authentication pattern.",
            "recommendation": {
