            "impact": "A caller who can reach the route could change whether a restaurant is marked active by choosing a `restaurant_id` in the URL. Depending on application use, that could alter restaurant availability or operational state for records other than the caller’s own tenant or for unauthenticated users.",
            "prerequisites": "- Exploitation depends on the `/admin/restaurants/<restaurant_id>/toggle` route being reachable to an attacker under the deployed configuration.\n- The trust-boundary context describes the admin blueprint as part of the public HTTP surface, reachable without prior authentication, and specifically lists `toggle_restaurant` at `app/routes/admin.py:15` as accepting attacker-chosen path input.\n- No evidence here indicates this is an optional extension or loadable module; it appears to be a normal Flask blueprint route in the application.\n- The trust boundary crossed is from an external web client to a privileged state-changing admin action on restaurant records.\n- The project’s supplied security concerns explicitly describe this admin route family as lacking authentication and role checks.\n- Related-known-pattern context: this matches the provided KB pattern for **CWE-862**, where an actor attempts a privileged action without an authorization check.\n- The state change itself appears to be by design for an administrative workflow; the question is whether access to that workflow is restricted server-side.",
            "recommendation": {
              "codeAfter": "from flask import Blueprint, abort, redirect, render_template, request, url_for\r\n\r\nfrom app import db\r\nfrom app.auth import current_user, login_required\r\n\r\nbp = Blueprint(\"admin\", __name__, url_prefix=\"/admin\")\r\n\r\n    return render_template(\"admin_restaurants.html\", restaurants=rows)\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.route(\"/restaurants/<int:restaurant_id>/toggle\", methods=[\"POST\"])\r\n@login_required\r\ndef toggle_restaurant(restaurant_id):\r\n    user = current_user()\r\n    if user is None or user[\"restaurant_id\"] != restaurant_id:\r\n        abort(403)\r\n\r\n    restaurant = db.get_restaurant(restaurant_id)\r\n    if restaurant is not None:\r\n        db.set_restaurant_active(restaurant_id, not restaurant[\"active\"])\r\n    return redirect(url_for(\"admin.restaurants\"))\r",
              "codeBefore": "from flask import Blueprint, redirect, render_template, request, url_for\r\n\r\nfrom app import db\r\n\r\nbp = Blueprint(\"admin\", __name__, url_prefix=\"/admin\")\r\n\r\n    return render_template(\"admin_restaurants.html\", restaurants=rows)\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.route(\"/restaurants/<int:restaurant_id>/toggle\", methods=[\"POST\"])\r\ndef toggle_restaurant(restaurant_id):\r\n    restaurant = db.get_restaurant(restaurant_id)\r\n    if restaurant is not None:\r\n        db.set_restaurant_active(restaurant_id, not restaurant[\"active\"])\r\n    return redirect(url_for(\"admin.restaurants\"))\r",
              "fixDiff": "--- a/app/routes/admin.py\n+++ b/app/routes/admin.py\n@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@\n-from flask import Blueprint, redirect, render_template, request, url_for\r\n-\r\n-from app import db\r\n+from flask import Blueprint, abort, redirect, render_template, request, url_for\r\n+\r\n+from app import db\r\n+from app.auth import current_user, login_required\r\n \r\n bp = Blueprint(\"admin\", __name__, url_prefix=\"/admin\")\r\n \r\n@@ -11,9 +12,14 @@\n     return render_template(\"admin_restaurants.html\", restaurants=rows)\r\n \r\n \r\n-@bp.route(\"/restaurants/<int:restaurant_id>/toggle\", methods=[\"POST\"])\r\n-def toggle_restaurant(restaurant_id):\r\n-    restaurant = db.get_restaurant(restaurant_id)\r\n-    if restaurant is not None:\r\n-        db.set_restaurant_active(restaurant_id, not restaurant[\"active\"])\r\n-    return redirect(url_for(\"admin.restaurants\"))\r\n+@bp.route(\"/restaurants/<int:restaurant_id>/toggle\", methods=[\"POST\"])\r\n+@login_required\r\n+def toggle_restaurant(restaurant_id):\r\n+    user = current_user()\r\n+    if user is None or user[\"restaurant_id\"] != restaurant_id:\r\n+        abort(403)\r\n+\r\n+    restaurant = db.get_restaurant(restaurant_id)\r\n+    if restaurant is not None:\r\n+        db.set_restaurant_active(restaurant_id, not restaurant[\"active\"])\r\n+    return redirect(url_for(\"admin.restaurants\"))",
              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn app/routes/admin.py, add authentication and an object-level authorization check to toggle_restaurant at line 15 so the route only proceeds for a logged-in user whose restaurant_id matches the target restaurant_id.\n\n### Suggested fix\nfrom flask import Blueprint, abort, redirect, render_template, request, url_for\r\n\r\nfrom app import db\r\nfrom app.auth import current_user, login_required\r\n\r\nbp = Blueprint(\"admin\", __name__, url_prefix=\"/admin\")\r\n\r\n    return render_template(\"admin_restaurants.html\", restaurants=rows)\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.route(\"/restaurants/<int:restaurant_id>/toggle\", methods=[\"POST\"])\r\n@login_required\r\ndef toggle_restaurant(restaurant_id):\r\n    user = current_user()\r\n    if user is None or user[\"restaurant_id\"] != restaurant_id:\r\n        abort(403)\r\n\r\n    restaurant = db.get_restaurant(restaurant_id)\r\n    if restaurant is not None:\r\n        db.set_restaurant_active(restaurant_id, not restaurant[\"active\"])\r\n    return redirect(url_for(\"admin.restaurants\"))\r\n\n### Rationale\nThe added login_required gate blocks unauthenticated requests, and comparing the session-backed principal to the URL target prevents the handler from using an arbitrary caller-supplied restaurant_id to select and update another restaurant's record.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, POST /admin/restaurants/2/toggle can toggle restaurant 2 when sent without a session or from a session associated with a different restaurant. After the change, unauthenticated requests should be rejected by the login guard and a logged-in user whose current_user()[\"restaurant_id\"] does not equal 2 should receive 403, while a matching authorized user can still toggle their own restaurant.",
              "remediationSteps": {
