            "impact": "An unauthenticated remote user could enumerate the restaurant records returned by this view, including identifiers, names, contact email addresses, and active/inactive status. If the endpoint is intended to be administrative, this exposes internal operational listing data to callers outside that trust boundary.",
            "prerequisites": "- The application must expose `GET /admin/restaurants` to remote clients without upstream protection such as reverse-proxy authentication.\n- The issue depends on the listing being intended for authenticated or administrative use; if it is meant to be public, the missing check is by design.\n- The trust boundary is a public unauthenticated web request crossing into an administrative route that returns database-backed restaurant records.\n- Based on the provided trust-boundary notes, these admin routes are part of the public web surface rather than an optional or loadable extension.\n- Project security notes explicitly call out the admin blueprint routes as lacking authentication or role checks.\n- No related CVE mapping was provided in the finding context.",
