              "fixDiff": "--- a/app/routes/admin.py\n+++ b/app/routes/admin.py\n@@ -1,14 +1,16 @@\n-from flask import Blueprint, redirect, render_template, request, url_for\r\n-\r\n-from app import db\r\n-\r\n-bp = Blueprint(\"admin\", __name__, url_prefix=\"/admin\")\r\n-\r\n-\r\n-@bp.route(\"/restaurants\")\r\n-def restaurants():\r\n-    rows = db.list_restaurants()\r\n-    return render_template(\"admin_restaurants.html\", restaurants=rows)\r\n+from flask import Blueprint, redirect, render_template, request, url_for\r\n+\r\n+from app import db\r\n+from app.auth import login_required\r\n+\r\n+bp = Blueprint(\"admin\", __name__, url_prefix=\"/admin\")\r\n+\r\n+\r\n+@bp.route(\"/restaurants\")\r\n+@login_required\r\n+def restaurants():\r\n+    rows = db.list_restaurants()\r\n+    return render_template(\"admin_restaurants.html\", restaurants=rows)\r\n \r\n \r\n @bp.route(\"/restaurants/<int:restaurant_id>/toggle\", methods=[\"POST\"])",
              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn app/routes/admin.py, import the existing login_required decorator and apply it to the restaurants() handler at line 9 so unauthenticated requests cannot reach the database read and template render.\n\n### Suggested fix\nfrom flask import Blueprint, redirect, render_template, request, url_for\r\n\r\nfrom app import db\r\nfrom app.auth import login_required\r\n\r\nbp = Blueprint(\"admin\", __name__, url_prefix=\"/admin\")\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.route(\"/restaurants\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef restaurants():\r\n    rows = db.list_restaurants()\r\n    return render_template(\"admin_restaurants.html\", restaurants=rows)\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.route(\"/restaurants/<int:restaurant_id>/toggle\", methods=[\"POST\"])\r\n\n### Rationale\nThe decorator enforces authentication before the route body executes, so anonymous HTTP clients cannot call db.list_restaurants() or receive the administrative listing. This moves the access-control decision to the server entry point instead of relying on route naming alone.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, request GET /admin/restaurants without a session cookie and observe that the response returns the restaurant listing page. After the change, repeat the same unauthenticated request and observe that the application redirects to login or otherwise denies access; then retry with a valid authenticated session and observe that the listing still renders for authorized users.",
