            "impact": "If these prerequisites hold, a third party can cause a logged-in user to be logged out without that user's intent. The direct effect described by the evidence is forced termination of the authenticated session rather than modification of account data.",
            "prerequisites": "- The application must use cookie-backed authentication, and the victim must already have an active authenticated session.\n- The victim's browser must send that session cookie on the cross-site request path used by the attacker; the transcript notes that this can still occur for top-level cross-site navigation.\n- The route appears in the main application code, not an optional extension.\n- The relevant trust boundary is **external web content to authenticated session state**: an attacker-controlled site can induce the victim browser to request `/logout`, and the server acts on the victim's ambient session.\n- The flagged behavior is partly by design in that the endpoint's purpose is to terminate a session; the issue is the combination of that state change with a default `GET` route and no request-origin proof.\n- No related CVE reference was provided in the finding context.",
            "recommendation": {
              "codeAfter": "from flask import (\r\n    Blueprint,\r\n    abort,\r\n    flash,\r\n    redirect,\r\n    render_template,\r\n    request,\r\n    url_for,\r\n)\r\n\r\nfrom app import auth, db\r\n\r\n    return render_template(\"login.html\")\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.route(\"/logout\", methods=[\"POST\"])\r\ndef logout():\r\n    origin = request.headers.get(\"Origin\")\r\n    referer = request.headers.get(\"Referer\")\r\n    expected = request.host_url.rstrip(\"/\")\r\n\r\n    if origin:\r\n        if origin.rstrip(\"/\") != expected:\r\n            abort(403)\r\n    elif referer:\r\n        if not referer.startswith(f\"{expected}/\") and referer.rstrip(\"/\") != expected:\r\n            abort(403)\r\n    else:\r\n        abort(403)\r\n\r\n    auth.logout_user()\r\n    return redirect(url_for(\"auth.login\"))\r",
