              "fixDiff": "--- a/app/routes/auth_routes.py\n+++ b/app/routes/auth_routes.py\n@@ -1,11 +1,12 @@\n-from flask import (\r\n-    Blueprint,\r\n-    flash,\r\n-    redirect,\r\n-    render_template,\r\n-    request,\r\n-    url_for,\r\n-)\r\n+from flask import (\r\n+    Blueprint,\r\n+    abort,\r\n+    flash,\r\n+    redirect,\r\n+    render_template,\r\n+    request,\r\n+    url_for,\r\n+)\r\n \r\n from app import auth, db\r\n \r\n@@ -25,7 +26,20 @@\n     return render_template(\"login.html\")\r\n \r\n \r\n-@bp.route(\"/logout\")\r\n-def logout():\r\n-    auth.logout_user()\r\n-    return redirect(url_for(\"auth.login\"))\r\n+@bp.route(\"/logout\", methods=[\"POST\"])\r\n+def logout():\r\n+    origin = request.headers.get(\"Origin\")\r\n+    referer = request.headers.get(\"Referer\")\r\n+    expected = request.host_url.rstrip(\"/\")\r\n+\r\n+    if origin:\r\n+        if origin.rstrip(\"/\") != expected:\r\n+            abort(403)\r\n+    elif referer:\r\n+        if not referer.startswith(f\"{expected}/\") and referer.rstrip(\"/\") != expected:\r\n+            abort(403)\r\n+    else:\r\n+        abort(403)\r\n+\r\n+    auth.logout_user()\r\n+    return redirect(url_for(\"auth.login\"))",
              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn app/routes/auth_routes.py, update the logout route at lines 28-30 to accept POST only and reject requests whose Origin or Referer is not same-origin before calling auth.logout_user(); add the needed abort import.\n\n### Suggested fix\nfrom flask import (\r\n    Blueprint,\r\n    abort,\r\n    flash,\r\n    redirect,\r\n    render_template,\r\n    request,\r\n    url_for,\r\n)\r\n\r\nfrom app import auth, db\r\n\r\n    return render_template(\"login.html\")\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.route(\"/logout\", methods=[\"POST\"])\r\ndef logout():\r\n    origin = request.headers.get(\"Origin\")\r\n    referer = request.headers.get(\"Referer\")\r\n    expected = request.host_url.rstrip(\"/\")\r\n\r\n    if origin:\r\n        if origin.rstrip(\"/\") != expected:\r\n            abort(403)\r\n    elif referer:\r\n        if not referer.startswith(f\"{expected}/\") and referer.rstrip(\"/\") != expected:\r\n            abort(403)\r\n    else:\r\n        abort(403)\r\n\r\n    auth.logout_user()\r\n    return redirect(url_for(\"auth.login\"))\r\n\n### Rationale\nRestricting logout to POST removes the browser's default cross-site navigation path to the state-changing endpoint, and checking same-origin request metadata adds origin proof before the session mutation occurs. Together these changes prevent a third-party site from triggering logout with only the victim's ambient session cookie.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, load a page on another origin that submits or navigates the victim browser to /logout and observe that the authenticated session is cleared and the browser is redirected to the login page. After the change, a direct cross-site GET should receive 405, and a cross-site POST with a foreign or missing Origin/Referer should receive 403 while a same-origin POST from the application should still log the user out.",
              "remediationSteps": {
                "description": "In app/routes/auth_routes.py, update the logout route at lines 28-30 to accept POST only and reject requests whose Origin or Referer is not same-origin before calling auth.logout_user(); add the needed abort import.",
                "rational": "Restricting logout to POST removes the browser's default cross-site navigation path to the state-changing endpoint, and checking same-origin request metadata adds origin proof before the session mutation occurs. Together these changes prevent a third-party site from triggering logout with only the victim's ambient session cookie.",
                "rationale": "Restricting logout to POST removes the browser's default cross-site navigation path to the state-changing endpoint, and checking same-origin request metadata adds origin proof before the session mutation occurs. Together these changes prevent a third-party site from triggering logout with only the victim's ambient session cookie.",
                "suggestedFix": "from flask import (\r\n    Blueprint,\r\n    abort,\r\n    flash,\r\n    redirect,\r\n    render_template,\r\n    request,\r\n    url_for,\r\n)\r\n\r\nfrom app import auth, db\r\n\r\n    return render_template(\"login.html\")\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.route(\"/logout\", methods=[\"POST\"])\r\ndef logout():\r\n    origin = request.headers.get(\"Origin\")\r\n    referer = request.headers.get(\"Referer\")\r\n    expected = request.host_url.rstrip(\"/\")\r\n\r\n    if origin:\r\n        if origin.rstrip(\"/\") != expected:\r\n            abort(403)\r\n    elif referer:\r\n        if not referer.startswith(f\"{expected}/\") and referer.rstrip(\"/\") != expected:\r\n            abort(403)\r\n    else:\r\n        abort(403)\r\n\r\n    auth.logout_user()\r\n    return redirect(url_for(\"auth.login\"))\r",
                "verification": "Before the change, load a page on another origin that submits or navigates the victim browser to /logout and observe that the authenticated session is cleared and the browser is redirected to the login page. After the change, a direct cross-site GET should receive 405, and a cross-site POST with a foreign or missing Origin/Referer should receive 403 while a same-origin POST from the application should still log the user out."
