            "severityRationale": "CVSS v3.1 base score 4.3 (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N, confidence: high) — AV:N (the shared trust boundary and validator evidence show /logout is a public HTTP route reachable over the network); AC:L (a cross-site GET directly reaches logout() and there is no CSRF token or origin validation on the path); PR:N (the attacker does not need an account to cause the victim browser to request /logout); UI:R (the victim must visit or trigger the attacker-controlled cross-site request so their browser sends the ambient session cookie); S:U (session.clear() changes authentication state only within the same web-application authority); C:N (no data disclosure is evidenced); I:L (auth.logout_user resolves to session.clear(), so the attacker causes an unauthorized but limited change to the victim’s authentication/session state); A:N (the evidence shows forced logout, not a broader loss of service availability).",
