            "dataFlowTrace": "`edit_item` -> `item` -> `db.update_menu_item`\n\n- **[ENTRY]** `edit_item`  `app/routes/menus.py:54`\n  The authenticated request supplies item_id in the route path, and the handler starts without verifying that the target record belongs to the caller's restaurant.\n- **[FLOW]** `item`  `app/routes/menus.py:55`\n  The handler reads the menu item for that item_id and does not compare any restaurant_id on the row to the current session identity.\n- **[FLAG]** `db.update_menu_item`  `app/routes/menus.py:64`\n  The same attacker-chosen item_id is forwarded into the update call together with edited fields, with no ownership check in this function.",
            "dataFlowValidation": "strict",
