            "severitySource": "validator",
            "summary": "`edit_item` handles `GET` and `POST` requests for `/menu/item/<item_id>/edit` and updates a menu item’s `name`, `price_cents`, and `available` fields. The flagged path accepts an attacker-controlled `item_id` and, after `@login_required`, loads and updates the record without checking that the target row belongs to the authenticated restaurant. This becomes a security issue if restaurant users are intended to be isolated from each other and can reach this route with another restaurant’s `item_id`.",
