              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn app/routes/menus.py, add an enabled-state check in dashboard() immediately after db.get_restaurant(...) at line 21, and import abort so the handler rejects requests for missing or inactive restaurants before loading dashboard data.\n\n### Suggested fix\nfrom flask import (\r\n    Blueprint,\r\n    abort,\r\n    flash,\r\n    redirect,\r\n    render_template,\r\n    request,\r\n    url_for,\r\n)\r\n\r\nfrom app import db\r\nfrom app.auth import current_user, login_required\r\n\r\n@bp.route(\"/dashboard\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef dashboard():\r\n    user = current_user()\r\n    restaurant = db.get_restaurant(user[\"restaurant_id\"])\r\n    if restaurant is None or not restaurant[\"active\"]:\r\n        abort(403)\r\n    items = db.list_menu_items(user[\"restaurant_id\"])\r\n    orders = db.list_orders(user[\"restaurant_id\"])\r\n    return render_template(\r\n        \"dashboard.html\",\r\n        restaurant=restaurant,\r\n        items=items,\r\n\n### Rationale\nChecking restaurant[\"active\"] before the menu and order queries prevents a session tied to a disabled tenant from being reused to authorize dashboard reads. Returning 403 stops the request before any tenant-scoped data is loaded or rendered.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, authenticate as a restaurant user, set that restaurant's active flag to false, keep the session cookie, and request GET /dashboard; the dashboard still renders restaurant, menu, and order data. After the change, the same request should return HTTP 403 with no dashboard data, while an active restaurant session should still load /dashboard normally.",
