            "annotatedSource": "# [ENTRY] The POST route is reachable by a client carrying a session cookie and an attacker-chosen order_id path parameter.\n72: def set_status(order_id):\n# [FLOW] The handler loads the current user identity from session-backed authentication and uses it as the tenant context.\n73:     user = current_user()\n74:     order = db.get_order(order_id)\n# [FLOW] Ownership is checked against user[\"restaurant_id\"], so the authorization decision depends on the trusted session-derived user.\n75:     if order is None or order[\"restaurant_id\"] != user[\"restaurant_id\"]:\n76:         flash(\"Order not found.\")\n77:         return redirect(url_for(\"orders.board\"))\n78: \n79:     new_status = request.form.get(\"status\", \"\")\n80:     if new_status not in ALLOWED_STATUSES:\n81:         flash(\"Unknown status.\")\n82:         return redirect(url_for(\"orders.board\"))\n83: \n# [FLAG] The scanner flagged the state-changing database update because it executes after authorization based on session-derived tenant identity.\n# [SINK] The order status is persisted here for the selected order_id after the preceding ownership check passes.\n>>>84:     db.update_order_status(order_id, new_status)\n85:     return redirect(url_for(\"orders.board\"))",
