            "cwe_display": "CWE-321: Use of Hard-coded Cryptographic Key",
            "cwe_name": "Use of Hard-coded Cryptographic Key",
            "dataFlowTrace": "`set_status` -> `current_user` -> `user[\"restaurant_id\"]` -> `db.update_order_status`\n\n- **[ENTRY]** `set_status`  `app/routes/orders.py:72`\n  A client sends POST /orders/<order_id>/status with ambient session state and an attacker-chosen order_id.\n- **[FLOW]** `current_user`  `app/routes/orders.py:73`\n  The handler obtains the authenticated user from session-backed identity without local revalidation of the tenant binding.\n- **[FLOW]** `user[\"restaurant_id\"]`  `app/routes/orders.py:75`\n  The order ownership check compares the order tenant to the session-derived user's restaurant_id before allowing the update path.\n- **[FLAG]** `db.update_order_status`  `app/routes/orders.py:84`\n  The flagged update executes if the preceding check accepts the session-derived tenant context.",
            "dataFlowValidation": "strict",
            "debateConsensus": "TP",
            "debateSummary": "- Review outcome in the provided transcript: **1 model classified the finding as true positive; 0 classified it as false positive**.\n- Main technical argument for the finding:\n  - `current_user()` trusts session data to identify the user.\n  - `set_status()` trusts the resulting `user[\"restaurant_id\"]` for tenant scoping before calling `db.update_order_status()`.\n  - If `SECRET_KEY` remains the known fallback `\"portal-dev-key\"`, Flask session integrity is weakened, making forged session cookies a prerequisite for cross-tenant status changes.\n- Main limiting argument raised in the transcript:\n  - The trigger description is imprecise about controlling `restaurant_id` directly; the more relevant control is over `session['user_id']`, from which the restaurant is derived.\n  - If deployments always override `SECRET_KEY`, the reported path does not cross the trust boundary described in the finding.\n- The debate record appears to be a single-model review with self-challenge rather than a multi-model split, so there is no separate opposing transcript.",
            "end_line": 84,
            "fileSourceUrl": "https://github.com/caldova-io/merchant-portal/blob/47bbff4de1fa369ff4fcac75139b2203096b29d1/app/routes/orders.py#L84",
