              "description": {
                "text": "### Description\nIn app/routes/orders.py, function survey_redirect at line 66, reject survey URLs that are not HTTPS before calling redirect().\n\n### Suggested fix\n        flash(\"Order not found.\")\r\n        return redirect(url_for(\"orders.board\"))\r\n\r\n    survey_url = hash1lib().build_customer_survey_url(order_id)\r\n    if not survey_url.startswith(\"https://\"):\r\n        flash(\"Survey unavailable.\")\r\n        return redirect(url_for(\"orders.board\"))\r\n    return redirect(survey_url)\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.route(\"/orders/<int:order_id>/status\", methods=[\"POST\"])\r\n\n### Rationale\nFailing closed on non-HTTPS destinations prevents this route from sending order-linked query data to an external endpoint over plaintext transport. The redirect only proceeds when the generated URL uses TLS.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, request /orders/<authorized_order_id>/survey and observe a 302 Location header pointing to an http:// survey URL. After the change, the same request should no longer redirect to a non-HTTPS destination; instead it should return the user to orders.board with the flash message, while an HTTPS survey URL would still be redirected."
              }
            }
