              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn app/routes/receipts.py in editor() at line 42, reject the save branch unless the request Origin or Referer matches the current application origin before calling db.set_receipt_template().\n\n### Suggested fix\n    preview = None\r\n    if request.method == \"POST\":\r\n        template = request.form.get(\"template\", \"\")\r\n        if request.form.get(\"action\") == \"save\":\r\n            expected_origin = request.host_url.rstrip(\"/\")\r\n            origin = request.headers.get(\"Origin\")\r\n            referer = request.headers.get(\"Referer\", \"\")\r\n            if origin:\r\n                if origin.rstrip(\"/\") != expected_origin:\r\n                    return (\"Forbidden\", 403)\r\n            elif referer != expected_origin and not referer.startswith(expected_origin + \"/\"):\r\n                return (\"Forbidden\", 403)\r\n            else:\r\n                return (\"Forbidden\", 403)\r\n            db.set_receipt_template(user[\"restaurant_id\"], template)\r\n            flash(\"Receipt template saved.\")\r\n        sample = db.list_orders(user[\"restaurant_id\"])\r\n        order = sample[0] if sample else None\r\n        preview = _render(template, order, restaurant)\r\n\n### Rationale\nAn origin check makes the state-changing POST depend on request metadata generated by the browser for the current site, so a cross-site form submission from another origin is not accepted for the receipt-template update.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, submit a POST to /receipts from an external site while the victim is logged in, with action=save and a chosen template; the server accepts the request and updates the stored receipt template. After the change, the same cross-site POST should return 403 and leave the existing template unchanged, while a same-origin form submission from the application should still save successfully.",
