            "severityRationale": "CVSS v3.1 base score 4.3 (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L, confidence: high) — AV:N (authenticated merchants reach the create/edit item handlers over HTTP and control the price field); AC:L (a non-finite price string like NaN or Infinity directly reaches normalize_price with no special environmental condition); PR:L (the affected create/edit routes are behind login_required); UI:N (the attacker submits the malformed form value themselves); S:U (the uncaught exception occurs inside the same Flask application authority); C:N (the evidence shows request failure, not data disclosure); I:N (the failing request prevents the save rather than directly modifying data); A:L (comparison, quantize, or int conversion on the non-finite Decimal can raise uncaught exceptions and make the create/edit request fail with a server error).",
