            "summary": "`normalize_price()` parses user-supplied price strings into integer cents for menu item create/edit flows. The scanner flagged line 28 because `Decimal(cleaned)` accepts non-finite strings such as `\"NaN\"` and `\"Infinity\"`, and the later comparison/quantize/int operations run outside the `try/except` that only handles parse failures. This becomes a security issue if an attacker can submit the `price` form field on the reachable create/edit routes; in the provided context, that boundary is an authenticated merchant session.",
