            "cwe_display": "CWE-250: Execution with Unnecessary Privileges",
            "cwe_name": "Execution with Unnecessary Privileges",
            "dataFlowTrace": "`FROM python:3.11-slim` -> `CMD`\n\n- **[FLOW]** `FROM python:3.11-slim`  `Dockerfile:1`\n  The build starts from a base image whose default runtime user is inherited unless a later USER instruction overrides it.\n- **[FLAG]** `CMD`  `Dockerfile:13`\n  The flagged startup command appears before any user change, so the container will execute it under the inherited default account.",
            "dataFlowValidation": "strict",
            "debateConsensus": "TP",
            "debateSummary": "- **True positive votes:** 1 analyzer transcript, plus the validator score marked the finding as real (`validator=100%`, `debate=100%`, combined `100%`)\n- **False positive votes:** 0\n- **Arguments supporting the finding:**\n  - The `Dockerfile` contains no `USER` instruction before the final `CMD`, so runtime identity is inherited from `python:3.11-slim`.\n  - The review notes a reachable in-repo server-side code-execution path through merchant-controlled Jinja template rendering in `app/routes/receipts.py` and `app/routes/orders.py`.\n  - Running the web process as root increases what post-exploitation code can modify inside the container, including application files and local writable data.\n- **Arguments raised against the finding:**\n  - Root inside a container is not the same as host root.\n  - Operators can override the runtime user outside the image.\n  - Exploitation depends on a separate application flaw, not the `Dockerfile` alone.\n- **Unresolved points:**\n  - Whether deployment policy already enforces a non-root runtime user is not shown in the repository.\n- **Review limitation:**\n  - The transcript shows a single analyzer with self-challenge rather than a visibly split multi-model debate.",
            "end_line": 13,
            "fileSourceUrl": "https://github.com/caldova-io/merchant-portal/blob/47bbff4de1fa369ff4fcac75139b2203096b29d1/Dockerfile#L13",
