              "fixDiff": "--- a/Dockerfile\n+++ b/Dockerfile\n@@ -6,8 +6,12 @@\n COPY merchant-portal/requirements.txt ./requirements.txt\r\n RUN pip install --no-index --find-links=/app/wheelhouse --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt\r\n \r\n-COPY merchant-portal/ ./\r\n-\r\n-EXPOSE 5000\r\n-\r\n-CMD [\"sh\", \"-c\", \"python migrations/init_db.py && python run.py\"]\r\n+COPY merchant-portal/ ./\r\n+\r\n+RUN useradd --create-home --shell /usr/sbin/nologin appuser \\\r\n+    && chown -R appuser:appuser /app\r\n+USER appuser\r\n+\r\n+EXPOSE 5000\r\n+\r\n+CMD [\"sh\", \"-c\", \"python migrations/init_db.py && python run.py\"]",
              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn Dockerfile at the startup section around line 13, create a dedicated unprivileged account, change ownership of /app to that account, and add a USER instruction before CMD so the Flask process does not run as the image default user.\n\n### Suggested fix\nCOPY merchant-portal/requirements.txt ./requirements.txt\r\nRUN pip install --no-index --find-links=/app/wheelhouse --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt\r\n\r\nCOPY merchant-portal/ ./\r\n\r\nRUN useradd --create-home --shell /usr/sbin/nologin appuser \\\r\n    && chown -R appuser:appuser /app\r\nUSER appuser\r\n\r\nEXPOSE 5000\r\n\r\nCMD [\"sh\", \"-c\", \"python migrations/init_db.py && python run.py\"]\r\n\n### Rationale\nAdding USER changes the runtime identity of the container process from the inherited root account to an unprivileged account. Chowning /app preserves the application's ability to initialize and write its local database while preventing server-side code execution in the web process from inheriting UID 0.\n\n### Verification\nBuild and start the image, then run `id -u` inside the running container or print `os.getuid()` from the Flask process. Before the change, the process reports `0` and an injected template payload executes as root. After the change, the process reports a non-zero UID, migrations still initialize the database under /app, and the same payload executes only with the unprivileged container account.",
              "remediationSteps": {
