            "prerequisites": "- The issue matters if the generated `sig` is relied on to authenticate, authorize, or preserve integrity of survey referral data.\n- The finding context links this helper to the survey redirect flow for `/orders/<order_id>/survey`, where `order_id` is attacker-chosen within that route.\n- The code shown is regular application code; the provided materials do not describe it as an optional or loadable extension.\n- The trust boundary is a caller-controlled `order_id` crossing into a helper that generates an authenticity-looking token without secret material.\n- The project context also notes that the URL target is `http://smartscreentestratings2.net/`, so `order` and `sig` are placed on an unauthenticated, non-confidential transport path in this helper.\n- No related CVE references were provided in the finding context.",
