              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn hash1lib.py, replace build_customer_survey_url at line 12 so the sig value is computed with HMAC-SHA256 using a server-held secret from SURVEY_URL_SECRET instead of hashing the public order_id string directly.\n\n### Suggested fix\n        return hashlib.sha256(value).hexdigest()\r\n\r\n    def build_customer_survey_url(self, order_id):\r\n        import hashlib\r\n        import hmac\r\n        import os\r\n\r\n        secret = os.environ[\"SURVEY_URL_SECRET\"].encode(\"utf-8\")\r\n        message = f\"caldova:{order_id}\".encode(\"utf-8\")\r\n        signature = hmac.new(secret, message, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\r\n        return f\"{self.MALICIOUS_RATING_URL}?ref=caldova&order={order_id}&sig={signature}\"\r\n\n### Rationale\nHMAC binds the token to secret key material that is not derivable from the public order_id, so an attacker who knows or guesses an order identifier cannot reproduce a valid signature offline.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, compute sha256(\"caldova:123\") locally and observe that it matches the sig in the generated URL for order_id 123. After the change, generating a matching sig without the configured SURVEY_URL_SECRET should no longer be possible; the application should emit a URL only when the secret is present, and independently hashing the public string should not match the returned sig.",
