              "codeBefore": "def create_app(config_object=Config):\r\n    app = Flask(__name__)\r\n    app.config.from_object(config_object)\r\n\r\n    db.init_app(app)\r\n\r\n    from app.routes.auth_routes import bp as auth_bp\r\n    from app.routes.menus import bp as menus_bp\r",
              "fixDiff": "--- a/app/__init__.py\n+++ b/app/__init__.py\n@@ -6,9 +6,15 @@\n \r\n def create_app(config_object=Config):\r\n     app = Flask(__name__)\r\n-    app.config.from_object(config_object)\r\n-\r\n-    db.init_app(app)\r\n+    app.config.from_object(config_object)\r\n+\r\n+    secret_key = app.config.get(\"SECRET_KEY\")\r\n+    if not secret_key or secret_key == \"portal-dev-key\":\r\n+        raise RuntimeError(\r\n+            \"MERCHANT_PORTAL_SECRET must be set to a non-default value before starting the app\"\r\n+        )\r\n+\r\n+    db.init_app(app)\r\n \r\n     from app.routes.auth_routes import bp as auth_bp\r\n     from app.routes.menus import bp as menus_bp",
              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn app/__init__.py within create_app at line 9, add a startup check after app.config.from_object(config_object) that rejects an empty SECRET_KEY or the built-in fallback value \"portal-dev-key\" before initializing the application.\n\n### Suggested fix\ndef create_app(config_object=Config):\r\n    app = Flask(__name__)\r\n    app.config.from_object(config_object)\r\n\r\n    secret_key = app.config.get(\"SECRET_KEY\")\r\n    if not secret_key or secret_key == \"portal-dev-key\":\r\n        raise RuntimeError(\r\n            \"MERCHANT_PORTAL_SECRET must be set to a non-default value before starting the app\"\r\n        )\r\n\r\n    db.init_app(app)\r\n\r\n    from app.routes.auth_routes import bp as auth_bp\r\n    from app.routes.menus import bp as menus_bp\r\n\n### Rationale\nFailing closed at startup prevents Flask from accepting a known or missing signing secret. Requiring an operator-supplied non-default SECRET_KEY means session cookies are signed with deployment-specific key material rather than a value embedded in the codebase.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, start the app with MERCHANT_PORTAL_SECRET unset and observe that it boots successfully using the fallback key. After the change, start the app with MERCHANT_PORTAL_SECRET unset or set to \"portal-dev-key\" and observe that startup raises the configured RuntimeError; then set MERCHANT_PORTAL_SECRET to a unique value and verify the app starts normally.",
              "remediationSteps": {
                "description": "In app/__init__.py within create_app at line 9, add a startup check after app.config.from_object(config_object) that rejects an empty SECRET_KEY or the built-in fallback value \"portal-dev-key\" before initializing the application.",
                "rational": "Failing closed at startup prevents Flask from accepting a known or missing signing secret. Requiring an operator-supplied non-default SECRET_KEY means session cookies are signed with deployment-specific key material rather than a value embedded in the codebase.",
                "rationale": "Failing closed at startup prevents Flask from accepting a known or missing signing secret. Requiring an operator-supplied non-default SECRET_KEY means session cookies are signed with deployment-specific key material rather than a value embedded in the codebase.",
                "suggestedFix": "def create_app(config_object=Config):\r\n    app = Flask(__name__)\r\n    app.config.from_object(config_object)\r\n\r\n    secret_key = app.config.get(\"SECRET_KEY\")\r\n    if not secret_key or secret_key == \"portal-dev-key\":\r\n        raise RuntimeError(\r\n            \"MERCHANT_PORTAL_SECRET must be set to a non-default value before starting the app\"\r\n        )\r\n\r\n    db.init_app(app)\r\n\r\n    from app.routes.auth_routes import bp as auth_bp\r\n    from app.routes.menus import bp as menus_bp\r",
