            "severityRationale": "CVSS v3.1 base score 6.5 (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N, confidence: medium) — AV:N (the shared trust boundary exposes the Flask app over public HTTP, and app/auth.py trusts session cookie fields once create_app loads Config with the fallback SECRET_KEY); AC:L (forging a Flask session signed with the known built-in key needs no race or special target state beyond that vulnerable configuration); PR:N (the attacker needs no existing account before sending a forged cookie); UI:N (the attacker can submit requests directly with the crafted session); S:U (the forged cookie is accepted by the same application security authority that loads users from session data); C:L (impersonation directly exposes the authenticated user’s portal data stored behind session-backed routes); I:L (the same impersonation directly enables user-level state changes on tenant data through authenticated routes); A:N (no direct service outage is evidenced).",
            "severitySource": "validator",
            "specificityGap": "[insecure-defaults] This is an insecure default. Default semantics exist because create_app defaults config_object to Config, and Config defines SECRET_KEY = os.environ.get(\"MERCHANT_PORTAL_SECRET\", \"portal-dev-key\"). The knob is security-sensitive because Flask SECRET_KEY protects session integrity. The default is unsafe because it is a hardcoded fallback secret, and there is no clear compensating guard such as dev-only gating or startup refusal when the default remains in use.",
            "summary": "`create_app()` defaults its `config_object` parameter to `Config` and loads that object with `app.config.from_object(config_object)` at `app/__init__.py:9`. The finding was flagged because `Config.SECRET_KEY` is reported to fall back to the hard-coded value `\"portal-dev-key\"` when `MERCHANT_PORTAL_SECRET` is unset. This becomes a security issue if the application is deployed with that fallback still active, because Flask uses `SECRET_KEY` to sign session cookies and related state.",
            "toolCategory": "IaC",
            "triggeringInputShape": "Operator leaves MERCHANT_PORTAL_SECRET unset, so create_app uses its default config_object=Config and loads Config.SECRET_KEY's fallback value \"portal-dev-key\".",
