                "rationale": "This change stops the code from deriving an authenticated identity from a Flask session cookie when the signing key is a known built-in constant. By refusing to trust session data under that configuration, forged cookies signed with the default key no longer produce a valid current_user().",
                "suggestedFix": "    session.clear()\r\n\r\n\r\ndef current_user():\r\n    from flask import current_app\r\n\r\n    if current_app.config.get(\"SECRET_KEY\") == \"portal-dev-key\":\r\n        session.clear()\r\n        g.user = None\r\n        return None\r\n\r\n    if \"user\" not in g:\r\n        user_id = session.get(\"user_id\")\r\n        g.user = db.get_user(user_id) if user_id else None\r\n    return g.user\r\n\r\n\r\ndef login_required(view):\r",
