            "debateSummary": "- **True positive votes:** 1\n- **False positive votes:** 0\n\n**TP arguments raised**\n- The bootstrap script reportedly inserts fixed email/password pairs for restaurant accounts.\n- The public login route passes submitted credentials into `verify_password()`.\n- Line 18 accepts any password that reproduces the stored hash, so unchanged seeded passwords remain usable for authentication.\n\n**FP arguments raised**\n- None in the transcript.\n\n**Unresolved points**\n- The issue depends on deployment choices: the initialization script must have been run, and the seeded passwords must still be present.\n\n**Review limitation**\n- The debate record shown here is a single-model review, so there was no adversarial multi-model disagreement to summarize.",
