            "function": "app/routes/auth_routes.py:login",
            "impact": "An external user could log in as one of the seeded restaurant accounts and gain whatever access that account has in the merchant portal. This includes access to session-backed routes and the data or actions authorized to that restaurant user.",
            "prerequisites": "- **Deployment conditions required:**\n  - The database must have been initialized through the shipped baseline seeding flow.\n  - The seeded accounts must still exist with their original passwords.\n  - The public `/login` route must be reachable by an unauthenticated user.\n- **Default vs optional path:** the finding summary states that `migrations/init_db.py seed()` inserts the accounts and that `main()` invokes that seeding during baseline initialization, so this is described as part of the normal bootstrap path rather than an optional extension.\n- **Trust boundary crossed:** an **unauthenticated remote web client** submits credentials to a public login route and can obtain an authenticated restaurant session if the known seeded credentials still work.\n- **Project context:** the provided trust-boundary notes classify `/login` as publicly reachable without prior authentication. The debate transcript also states that the startup flow and README expose the demo credentials. The related reference supplied for this finding is a generic **CWE-798 hard-coded/default-credentials pattern**, not a named CVE tied to this project.",
            "recommendation": {
              "codeAfter": "@bp.route(\"/login\", methods=[\"GET\", \"POST\"])\r\ndef login():\r\n    if request.method == \"POST\":\r\n        email = request.form.get(\"email\", \"\").strip().lower()\r\n        password = request.form.get(\"password\", \"\")\r\n        user = db.get_user_by_email(email)\r\n        default_credentials = {\r\n            (\"owner@b021bistro.io\", \"bistro123\"),\r\n            (\"owner@noodlebot.io\", \"noodle123\"),\r\n        }\r\n        if (email, password) in default_credentials:\r\n            flash(\"Invalid email or password.\")\r\n        elif user and auth.verify_password(user, password):\r\n            auth.login_user(user)\r\n            return redirect(url_for(\"menus.dashboard\"))\r\n        else:\r\n            flash(\"Invalid email or password.\")\r\n    return render_template(\"login.html\")\r\n\r\n\r",
              "codeBefore": "@bp.route(\"/login\", methods=[\"GET\", \"POST\"])\r\ndef login():\r\n    if request.method == \"POST\":\r\n        email = request.form.get(\"email\", \"\").strip().lower()\r\n        password = request.form.get(\"password\", \"\")\r\n        user = db.get_user_by_email(email)\r\n        if user and auth.verify_password(user, password):\r\n            auth.login_user(user)\r\n            return redirect(url_for(\"menus.dashboard\"))\r\n        flash(\"Invalid email or password.\")\r\n    return render_template(\"login.html\")\r\n\r\n\r",
              "fixDiff": "--- a/app/routes/auth_routes.py\n+++ b/app/routes/auth_routes.py\n@@ -14,14 +14,21 @@\n \r\n @bp.route(\"/login\", methods=[\"GET\", \"POST\"])\r\n def login():\r\n-    if request.method == \"POST\":\r\n-        email = request.form.get(\"email\", \"\").strip().lower()\r\n-        password = request.form.get(\"password\", \"\")\r\n-        user = db.get_user_by_email(email)\r\n-        if user and auth.verify_password(user, password):\r\n-            auth.login_user(user)\r\n-            return redirect(url_for(\"menus.dashboard\"))\r\n-        flash(\"Invalid email or password.\")\r\n+    if request.method == \"POST\":\r\n+        email = request.form.get(\"email\", \"\").strip().lower()\r\n+        password = request.form.get(\"password\", \"\")\r\n+        user = db.get_user_by_email(email)\r\n+        default_credentials = {\r\n+            (\"owner@b021bistro.io\", \"bistro123\"),\r\n+            (\"owner@noodlebot.io\", \"noodle123\"),\r\n+        }\r\n+        if (email, password) in default_credentials:\r\n+            flash(\"Invalid email or password.\")\r\n+        elif user and auth.verify_password(user, password):\r\n+            auth.login_user(user)\r\n+            return redirect(url_for(\"menus.dashboard\"))\r\n+        else:\r\n+            flash(\"Invalid email or password.\")\r\n     return render_template(\"login.html\")",
              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn app/routes/auth_routes.py within login() at lines 17-24, block authentication attempts that use the shipped seeded email/password pairs before calling auth.verify_password() and auth.login_user().\n\n### Suggested fix\n@bp.route(\"/login\", methods=[\"GET\", \"POST\"])\r\ndef login():\r\n    if request.method == \"POST\":\r\n        email = request.form.get(\"email\", \"\").strip().lower()\r\n        password = request.form.get(\"password\", \"\")\r\n        user = db.get_user_by_email(email)\r\n        default_credentials = {\r\n            (\"owner@b021bistro.io\", \"bistro123\"),\r\n            (\"owner@noodlebot.io\", \"noodle123\"),\r\n        }\r\n        if (email, password) in default_credentials:\r\n            flash(\"Invalid email or password.\")\r\n        elif user and auth.verify_password(user, password):\r\n            auth.login_user(user)\r\n            return redirect(url_for(\"menus.dashboard\"))\r\n        else:\r\n            flash(\"Invalid email or password.\")\r\n    return render_template(\"login.html\")\r\n\r\n\r\n\n### Rationale\nRejecting the known seeded credential pairs at the public login boundary prevents the application from accepting out-of-box passwords as valid authentication secrets, even if those seeded accounts remain in the database.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, submit POST /login with owner@b021bistro.io / bistro123 or owner@noodlebot.io / noodle123 and observe that the handler establishes a session and redirects to menus.dashboard. After the change, the same requests should stay on the login page and return the generic invalid-credentials message, while a non-default account with a valid password should still authenticate successfully.",
              "remediationSteps": {
                "description": "In app/routes/auth_routes.py within login() at lines 17-24, block authentication attempts that use the shipped seeded email/password pairs before calling auth.verify_password() and auth.login_user().",
                "rational": "Rejecting the known seeded credential pairs at the public login boundary prevents the application from accepting out-of-box passwords as valid authentication secrets, even if those seeded accounts remain in the database.",
                "rationale": "Rejecting the known seeded credential pairs at the public login boundary prevents the application from accepting out-of-box passwords as valid authentication secrets, even if those seeded accounts remain in the database.",
