              "description": {
                "text": "### Description\nIn app/routes/auth_routes.py within login() at lines 17-24, block authentication attempts that use the shipped seeded email/password pairs before calling auth.verify_password() and auth.login_user().\n\n### Suggested fix\n@bp.route(\"/login\", methods=[\"GET\", \"POST\"])\r\ndef login():\r\n    if request.method == \"POST\":\r\n        email = request.form.get(\"email\", \"\").strip().lower()\r\n        password = request.form.get(\"password\", \"\")\r\n        user = db.get_user_by_email(email)\r\n        default_credentials = {\r\n            (\"owner@b021bistro.io\", \"bistro123\"),\r\n            (\"owner@noodlebot.io\", \"noodle123\"),\r\n        }\r\n        if (email, password) in default_credentials:\r\n            flash(\"Invalid email or password.\")\r\n        elif user and auth.verify_password(user, password):\r\n            auth.login_user(user)\r\n            return redirect(url_for(\"menus.dashboard\"))\r\n        else:\r\n            flash(\"Invalid email or password.\")\r\n    return render_template(\"login.html\")\r\n\r\n\r\n\n### Rationale\nRejecting the known seeded credential pairs at the public login boundary prevents the application from accepting out-of-box passwords as valid authentication secrets, even if those seeded accounts remain in the database.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, submit POST /login with owner@b021bistro.io / bistro123 or owner@noodlebot.io / noodle123 and observe that the handler establishes a session and redirects to menus.dashboard. After the change, the same requests should stay on the login page and return the generic invalid-credentials message, while a non-default account with a valid password should still authenticate successfully."
              }
            }
