            "prerequisites": "- The `migrations/init_db.py` bootstrap path must be executed to create or recreate the database.\n- The seeded user records must remain present and their passwords must not be changed before exposure to users.\n- The application's login route must be reachable; the matching security context references `app/routes/auth_routes.py:16` and related auth helpers as the authentication path that consumes these records.\n- This is a Python bootstrap script, not an optional compiled extension, but it runs only when the initialization workflow is invoked.\n- The trust boundary is:\n  - local operator/CI/container startup process seeds the database, then\n  - unauthenticated remote clients can attempt login using the shipped credentials.\n- Project context notes describe this bootstrap as appearing intended for local/demo setup, and the risk depends on whether those defaults survive into attacker-reachable environments.\n- The pattern matches the listed **KB Pattern (CWE-798)** for hard-coded/default credentials; no specific CVE was provided for this code.",
